	<item>
		<title>AI in Cyber and Software Security:  What’s Driving Opportunities and Risks?</title>
		<link>https://dfrlab.org/2024/08/19/ai-in-cyber-and-software-security-opportunities-and-risks/</link>
		<pubDate>Mon, 19 Aug 2024 10:31:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Artificial Intelligence]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cyber Statecraft Initiative]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Cybersecurity]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Issue briefs and reports]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://dfrlab.org/?p=230050888</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>This issue brief discusses the drivers of evolving risks and opportunities presented by generative artificial intelligence (GAI), particularly in cybersecurity, while acknowledging the broader implications for policymakers and for national security.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://dfrlab.org/2024/08/19/ai-in-cyber-and-software-security-opportunities-and-risks/">AI in Cyber and Software Security:  What’s Driving Opportunities and Risks?</a> appeared first on <a href="https://dfrlab.org">DFRLab</a>.</p>
]]></description>
					
		
		
